d-ddc20d2164b144c2","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final and post-restart evidence. The LDAP directory is operational and persistent, node2 finds both unchanged users, write authorization behaves correctly, and the OS/kernel constraint was preserved. Operational hygiene is reduced by two temporary failed password mutations and one abandoned template file, but these do not undermine task functionality.","limitations":["The lifecycle snapshot shows /tmp/branch.inf still present on node1, while the executor's cleanup checks only covered /root/branch.inf and selected /run files; therefore the final report's broad temporary-file cleanup claim is not fully supported.","The captured evidence establishes final directory values and an unchanged source checksum, but it does not provide a generalized attribute-by-attribute comparison beyond the staged entries shown in the supplied LDIF."]}
